  [1mAlgorithm[0m ([38;5;153mtruncateWords(str, maxLength)[39m, a module-local helper in the same file):

  1. [38;5;153mstr.length <= maxLength[39m → return unchanged, no ellipsis.
  2. [38;5;153mmaxLength <= 3[39m → return [38;5;153m'...'.slice(0, maxLength)[39m; there's no room for content.
  3. Otherwise take the first [38;5;153mmaxLength - 3[39m characters, cut back to the last space in that window, [38;5;153mtrimEnd()[39m it, and
     append [38;5;153m'...'[39m. If the window has no space — a URL, a hash, an unspaced script — fall back to the hard cut at
     [38;5;153mmaxLength - 3[39m. Output is always ≤ [38;5;153mmaxLength[39m.

  [1mFiles touched:[0m [38;5;153mformat.js[39m (the block plus the helper), [38;5;153mformat.test.js[39m (new [38;5;153mconsole.assert[39m lines in the existing style).

  [1mTesting:[0m short string untouched; clean cut at a space; long-word fallback; no-space input; [38;5;153mmaxLength[39m at and just below
  the ellipsis boundary (3 and 4); interaction with [38;5;153mprefix[39m so the prefix survives. Run with [38;5;153mnode format.test.js[39m —
